## Hypotheses already in the ledger (do not duplicate)
- After 3+ straight losses, players underperform their rating (tilt).
- After 3+ straight wins, players overperform their rating (hot hand).
- Rapid-fire games started within 3 minutes after a loss underperform.
- The first game of a session is worse than later games, because the player is not warmed up.
- Very long sessions (index 25+) show fatigue and lower residuals.
- Late-night games (UTC 0-5) underperform a player's daytime games.
- After the previous game ended on time forfeit, the next game is worse.
- White's advantage is larger for 2400+ players than for others.
- Players rated 50+ above their opponent underperform the Elo expectation.
- Arena tournament games produce different residuals than pool games for 1600-2000 players.
- A very heavy day (30+ games played today) lowers performance.
- Playing on weekends differs from weekdays for 1200-1600 players.
- Start-minute parity has no effect (placebo).
- After the previous game was abandoned, performance drops.
- After a loss streak, a cool-off break of 30+ minutes recovers performance relative to immediate continuation.
- Low-rated players (<1200) score better with an increment (180+2) than in 180+0 games.
- Black players in the 1600-2000 band score worse with D-family (queen's pawn) openings.
- After a win against a higher-rated opponent, the next game is overperformed (momentum).
- 2000-2400 players do worse than usual when facing opponents rated 2400+.

